  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><munder><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></mrow></munder><mo>=</mo><munder><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></mrow></munder></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>From the graph, we have</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0113_c835eecbbf27.png\" style=\"width: 311px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>It is clear from the graph that the two graphs have only one point of intersection.</p><p>So, number of real roots of the given equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
